<!-- Website teaching layer for kotlin.md (the Kotlin learning path). -->

<!-- @opening -->
<p class="story-lead">Most Kotlin bugs that reach production are not syntax mistakes. A <code>val</code> that wasn't immutable, a platform type that was secretly null, a lambda that kept a screen alive, a flow that dropped values nobody meant to drop. Each one comes from a mental model that stopped one layer too early.</p>

This path builds those layers in order: first **values and types you can trust**, then **what the compiler does with your code**, then **asynchronous work that can be cancelled and tested**, and finally **what runs on the JVM and Android runtime**. Every chapter starts from a concrete problem and ends with the decisions a staff engineer makes about it.

<!-- @diagram 4b9b13a8f264b658 -->
### The route through Kotlin

<figure class="viz"><div class="viz-stack"><div class="node"><strong>Before you start: Engineering Fundamentals</strong><small>immutability, state machines, backpressure</small></div><div class="down"></div><div class="viz-grid" data-cols="3"><div class="node is-key"><strong>1 · Language core</strong><small>8 chapters · values, nulls, functions, data, sealed types, delegation</small></div><div class="node is-key"><strong>2 · Type system</strong><small>2 chapters · generics and variance for safe APIs</small></div><div class="node is-key"><strong>3 · Compiler features</strong><small>2 chapters · inlining and reified types</small></div><div class="node is-key"><strong>4 · Coroutines and Flow</strong><small>6 chapters · suspension, cancellation, streams, testing</small></div><div class="node is-key"><strong>5 · Runtime and JVM</strong><small>3 chapters · memory, Java interop, bytecode</small></div><div class="node"><strong>6 · Current release</strong><small>1 chapter · re-check with each Kotlin version</small></div></div></div><figcaption>Phases build on each other: stable mental models first, version-specific details last, so a new release adds to what you know instead of replacing it.</figcaption></figure>
